<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/integration.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/integration.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/integration.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You compare classes from two {{domain}} domain ontologies that were built separately from different literature (for example techno-economic analysis and reliability). Each input row is a candidate pair with an id, class A and class B. Each class has a label, its domain, its BFO kind, its parent and a definition (often blank). match is "=" when the two names (or a synonym) are the same after normalization, otherwise the similarity of the names (0-1).

For each pair choose one relation of A to B:
- equivalent: the same concept and the same kind of entity, so every instance of A is a B and every B is an A
- exact: the same concept, but the two domains may model it as a different kind of entity
- close: overlapping meaning, interchangeable in some uses but not all
- broader: A is a more general concept than B (B is a kind of A)
- narrower: A is a more specific concept than B (A is a kind of B)
- none: different concepts, including ones that only share a word ("module cost" is not "module"), a measured quantity versus the thing it is measured on {{ex:measured_thing}}, or an abbreviation that stands for different things in the two domains

Judge from the labels, kinds, parents and definitions together. The same name in two domains usually means the same concept, but not always. Use equivalent or exact only when you are confident; when unsure prefer close or none.

Return ONLY JSON matching the schema, with one entry per input id.

SCHEMA
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "1fe96b81427cecb5d112c3d4b3d4e3f62b9d39c8d53fbe69013f9e086582994b" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/integration.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You align classes of a {{domain}} ontology with terms from external ontologies (BFO, CCO, RO, QUDT, PMDCO, IOF, MDS-Onto). Each input class has a label, definition and parent, plus numbered candidate terms retrieved for it from the ontology store, as [n, label, ontology, definition, match] or [n, label, ontology, definition, match, "via k hop(s)"]. match is "=" when the candidate's name matches the class name or a synonym, otherwise the search score (0-1). "via k hop(s)" marks a candidate reached through the mappings of another candidate; judge it on its own meaning.

For each class, choose zero or more candidates and a relation:
- equivalent: same meaning and same kind of entity
- exact: same meaning, but the two ontologies may model it as different kinds of entity
- close: similar meaning, interchangeable in some uses
- broader: the candidate is a broader kind of thing than the class ("Voltage" for "open-circuit voltage")
- narrower: the candidate is a more specific kind of thing than the class
- related: associated in meaning but neither the same nor broader or narrower
Leave out wrong or unrelated candidates (relation none), including ones that only share a word ("carrier-induced degradation" is not "Armored Personnel Carrier"). Use exact or equivalent only when the names match ("=") and the meanings agree; otherwise use close, broader, narrower or related. QUDT quantity kinds and units are individuals: never equivalent for them.

Return ONLY JSON matching the schema.

SCHEMA
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "d50dde7ec7800f5906349fe9562da5598a2a0a207ef791241072c1dace13db90" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/interoperability_filter.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/interoperability_filter.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/interoperability_filter.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You screen candidate terms from external ontologies for {{domain}} ontology classes. Each class has numbered candidates retrieved from the ontology store as [n, label, ontology, definition, match] (match is "=" for a name match, else the search score 0-1; a sixth entry "via k hop(s)" marks a candidate reached through another candidate's mappings).
For each class return the numbers of the candidates that are about the SAME thing, a broader or narrower kind of it, or a closely related thing. Reject candidates that only share a word ("carrier-induced degradation" is not "Armored Personnel Carrier") or name a different thing. Return an empty list when none fits.

Return ONLY this JSON, with one entry for every class id you were given (an empty list when no candidate fits), for example:
{"keep":[{"id":"k0","candidates":[1,3]},{"id":"k00","candidates":[]}]}
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "8212222cdb36ffaab2a3eeaa0c604586b56ad88a0dc4425934b237469097918f" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/interoperability_filter.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/normalization.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/normalization.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/normalization.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You settle synonym candidates for a {{domain}} concept list. Each cluster holds terms that an embedding model found similar. Merge only terms that name the SAME concept: synonyms, acronyms, spelling or inflection variants. Do NOT merge broader and narrower terms (for example "defect" and "crack"), a quantity with its unit, a thing with its property, or opposite terms.

Return ONLY JSON: {"merges":[{"ids":[...],"label":"preferred label"}]}. Each merge uses ids from ONE cluster and has at least 2 ids. The preferred label is the clearest full name (not an acronym). Omit clusters where nothing should merge.

SCHEMA
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "7ca8776487cf23eecd9dbecec099c81ab8a3046086553c5b62102edd281f9e31" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/normalization.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/normalization_summary.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/normalization_summary.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/normalization_summary.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You write the summary section of a corpus report for a set of {{domain}} research papers. The input gives the highest-ranked concepts (with importance tier, paper count and mention count), the best-supported causal claims, and the longest causal chains.

Return ONLY JSON:
- summary: 2 short paragraphs on what the corpus is about, which concepts dominate, and which causal mechanisms recur. Use only the input. No claims beyond it.
- themes: 3-7 thematic groups, each with a short name and the input concept labels that belong to it.

SCHEMA
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "9ee8cd62285c8a6159492ed838bd0eb0b2b8a7f5f326d43f5193318b9191c5e1" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/normalization_summary.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/normalization_types.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/normalization_types.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/normalization_types.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You settle the type of {{domain}} concepts that different papers typed differently. For each input concept choose exactly one type from its "types" options, the one that fits the concept as most papers use it.
material/device/equipment = physical things; process = something that happens (a step or event); parameter = a setting of a process; property/quantity = a measurable characteristic; phenomenon = a physical effect or mechanism; method = a technique or procedure; defect = a physical flaw or failure mode; condition = a stressor or environment; information = data, models, standards.

Return ONLY JSON matching the schema.

SCHEMA
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "bba1eb33151941abda9185718f69c61b0155ad352513c83a03d329f0061a7ab4" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/normalization_types.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/ontology.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/ontology.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/ontology.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You place {{domain}} concepts in a BFO 2020 / Common Core Ontologies (CCO) class hierarchy.

For each input concept choose exactly one parent:
- "U:<label>" = one of the concept's "candidates" (CCO and BFO classes retrieved for that concept from the ontology store, most specific first), or a category from BFO CATEGORIES, or
- a concept id (k<n>) from CORPUS CONCEPTS, when the concept is truly a kind of that concept (every instance of the child is an instance of the parent).
Pick the most specific correct parent. Choose a corpus concept over an external class whenever a true is-a holds. Never invent a class that is not listed.

BFO guidance:
- material entity: things with mass ({{ex:material_entities}}); an amount of a substance or an engineered object goes under the candidate that names that kind of material entity.
- quality: a measurable property that inheres in a bearer ({{ex:onto_quality}}). This is the property itself, not a measured value.
- disposition / function: a capacity realized in processes ({{ex:onto_function}}).
- process: something that unfolds in time ({{ex:onto_process}}).
- information (generically dependent continuant): data, models, metrics as information, measurement values, standards, test protocols and plans.
- A quality never goes under a material entity. A process never goes under a continuant. A defect that is a physical feature (crack, void) is a material entity or site; a defect that is a tendency is a disposition.

Set "exclude": true only for items that should not be classes: a specific sample or dataset name, a single numeric value, a person or organization, a paper-specific label.

Return ONLY JSON matching the schema.

SCHEMA

Use source_definitions and relationship evidence as context, not universal definitions. Distinguish a general concept from an experimental configuration or particular specimen. Prefer a corpus parent supported by verified is_a evidence when categories agree; part_of and made_of are not is_a. Flagged or conditional source claims require caution; quote verification alone does not establish universal truth.
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "07a1c01ddef1459a660d8f35a44be9410f1cbea8a279028bcec3f3e070d08dd8" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/ontology.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/ontology_category.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/ontology_category.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/ontology_category.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You assign each {{domain}} concept to ONE BFO category from CATEGORIES, or "not a class".
- material entity: things with mass ({{ex:material_entities}}, physical defects like cracks).
- site: a location or cavity defined by material things (interface region, void).
- quality: a measurable property inhering in something ({{ex:cat_quality}}).
- disposition: a tendency or susceptibility ({{ex:cat_disposition}}).
- function: what an artifact is designed to do ({{ex:cat_function}}).
- role: a part something plays in a context (dopant role, test specimen).
- process: something that unfolds in time (degradation, annealing, deposition, measurement, exposure).
- process profile: a characteristic of a process such as a rate, temperature profile or process parameter.
- information: data, models, metrics as information, standards, protocols, reports.
- not a class: a specific sample or dataset name, a single number, a person or organization, a paper-specific label.

Return ONLY JSON matching the schema.

SCHEMA

Use source_definitions and relationship evidence as context, not universal definitions. Distinguish a general concept from an experimental configuration or particular specimen. Prefer a corpus parent supported by verified is_a evidence when categories agree; part_of and made_of are not is_a. Flagged or conditional source claims require caution; quote verification alone does not establish universal truth.
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "e73bbce794e51075c89aaae4c56df8515064a9c06086ae3d6d4ed652282a1c91" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/ontology_category.md" .

<https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        kw:ResourceSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md" ;
    skos:definition "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."@en ;
    kw:definitionStatus "source-derived description" ;
    kw:resourceKind "prompt" ;
    kw:resourceText """You choose the parent class for {{domain}} concepts that were already assigned the BFO category shown in CATEGORY.
Choose exactly one parent per concept:
- "U:<label>" = one of the concept's "candidates" (CCO and BFO classes of this category retrieved for that concept from the ontology store), or
- a concept id (k<n>) from the concept's "corpus" list (the corpus concepts of this category nearest to it), or from CORPUS CONCEPTS when that list is given, when the concept is truly a kind of it (every instance of the child is an instance of the parent).
Pick the most specific correct parent; prefer a corpus concept whenever a true is-a holds. Never invent a class that is not listed.
If the category shown is clearly wrong for a concept, answer "U:<category>" with the correct category from OTHER CATEGORIES instead.

Return ONLY JSON matching the schema.

SCHEMA

Use source_definitions and relationship evidence as context, not universal definitions. Distinguish a general concept from an experimental configuration or particular specimen. Prefer a corpus parent supported by verified is_a evidence when categories agree; part_of and made_of are not is_a. Flagged or conditional source claims require caution; quote verification alone does not establish universal truth.
""" ;
    kw:sourceDigest "5f9146f08c9ad6146ee6df0c3d306ea08c0f73f21b401c19b9704cfcb9058c73" ;
    kw:sourcePath "src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md" .

